  "content": {
    "id": "p38-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "The rate of growth of a certain town's population is proportional to the excess of the population over 10000. If the town initially has 18000 people and after 4 years the population grows to 25000, find how long it would take to do each of the following. Give times to the nearest 0.1 year.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p38-q10-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Reach 40000.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "8.4 years",
          "worked": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p38-q10-answer-intro",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Using ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "P=10000+Ae^{kt}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", with t in years:",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p38-q10-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\begin{aligned}18000&=10000+A\\\\A&=8000\\\\25000&=10000+8000e^{4k}\\\\15000&=8000e^{4k}\\\\e^{4k}&=\\frac{15}{8}\\\\k&=\\frac14\\ln\\left(\\frac{15}{8}\\right)\\\\P(t)&=10000+8000e^{kt}\\\\40000&=10000+8000e^{kt}\\\\30000&=8000e^{kt}\\\\e^{kt}&=\\frac{15}{4}\\\\t&=\\frac{\\ln(\\frac{15}{4})}{k}\\\\t&\\approx8.4\\text{ years}\\end{aligned}",
                    "display": true
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 57
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q10-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Be double the initial population.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "7.5 years",
          "worked": "Double the initial population is $2\\times18000=36000$. Using $P(t)=10000+8000e^{kt}$, where $k=\\frac14\\ln\\left(\\frac{15}{8}\\right)$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}36000&=10000+8000e^{kt}\\\\26000&=8000e^{kt}\\\\e^{kt}&=\\frac{13}{4}\\\\t&=\\frac{\\ln(13/4)}{k}\\\\t&\\approx7.5\\text{ years}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
  },
